{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>וארא.</b> The prophecy of the patriarchs was in night visions; therefore the word וארא." "The word \"Shaddai\" is difficult in interpretation. The Gaon [Saadia] said that the shin is added like the shin of \"שאתה מדבר עמי\" (Judges 6:17), and the meaning is that He said to the world, \"enough [dai].\" But I do not know the reason for this interpretation, for how can a name meaning \"enough\" be only an epithet, like \"טוב וסלח\" (Psalms 86:5), \"עלי לבי דַוָי\" (Jeremiah 5:8)? And the Nagid R. Samuel interpreted it in the Arabic tongue as al-qahhar, and explained it as \"victorious and mighty,\" the yod being in place of the doubling letter, like the yod in \"דַלְיוֹ שֹּׁקַיִם מִפִסֵח\" (Proverbs 26:7), and the alef in \"אשר בזאו נהרים\" (Isaiah 18:2). And like it: \"כקול שדי\" (Ezekiel 1:24), \"והיה שדי בצריך\" (Job 22:25). And he interpreted well." "And the word נודעתי is from the nif'al binyan, and it is not like הודעתי, per the words of Menachem." "And R. Marinus said that ושמי ד׳ is an oath, for in the Arabic tongue there is a vav of oath, and the meaning of לא נודעתי להם is \"as I made myself known to you,\" and this vav we do not find in the holy tongue [Leshon ha-Kodesh], and thus is his grammar: there are words that pull themselves and others along with them, likewise letters such as mem: \"מאל אביך ויעזרך, ואת שדי\" (Genesis 49:25), which is מאת שדי, and likewise the bet in באל שדי, as if written ובשמי ד׳ לא נודעתי להם." "Rav Saadia the Gaon said that at the end the word לבדו is missing, as if it said: ובשמי ד׳ לבדו לא נודעתי להם — but only at times by El Shaddai and at times by the name YHWH. And its parallel, in my opinion: לא יעקב לבדו — it will no longer be said that your name is Jacob, but rather Israel participates with him. And there is no need for this emendation, for we know that El Shaddai is the honored Name, blessed be He, and there is no difference between them, except that the name Shaddai is an epithet and the honored Name is sometimes a proper noun and sometimes an epithet, as I have explained. And behold, we find written concerning Abraham: \"אני ד' אשר הוצאתיך מאור כשדים\" (Genesis 15:7), and concerning Jacob: \"אני ד' אלהי אברהם אביך\" (ibid. 28:13). And R. Yeshua said that Abraham and Jacob did not know this name; rather, Moses wrote it thus. And R. Yeshua's words are not correct, for how could Moses write a name without the name having been mentioned [to them]? And there is no doubt that the patriarchs knew this name, which is the proper noun; rather, this name as an epithet they did not know." "And now I will reveal to you something of the secret of El Shaddai. We know that HaShem created three worlds, as I have mentioned, and the lower world receives power from the middle world, each particular according to the arrangement of the supernal. And because the soul of man is higher than the middle world, if the soul is wise and recognizes the deeds of HaShem, which are both without intermediary and by means of intermediary, and it abandons the desires of the lower world and cleaves to the honored Name — if there is in the arrangement of the stars at the time of conception an evil decreed to come upon a person on a known day, HaShem, to whom he cleaves, will bring about causes to save him from its evil. And likewise, if there is in the arrangement that he will be barren, HaShem will repair his generative power and he will beget. Therefore the Sages, blessed be their memory, said that HaShem said to Abraham: Depart from your astrology. And close to this reason is: There is no mazal for Israel. And I will further explain this in the section of Ki Tissa. Therefore HaShem said to Abraham before \"וארבה את זרעך\": \"אני אל שדי\" (Genesis 17:1), which means: the conqueror of the supernal arrangements — not that the arrangement is destroyed, but rather that the one who cleaves to His name knows that He will innovate good for him that is not in his arrangement. Therefore Jacob said: \"המלאך הגואל אותי מכל רע\" (ibid. 48), for evil was ready to come upon him. And this is the secret of the entire Torah, as I will yet explain. And behold, the patriarchs did not reach the level of cleaving to the Name like Moses, who knew HaShem face to face. Therefore Moses was able to change the phenomena of the lower world and to bring about signs and wonders that the patriarchs could not bring about. And behold, Moses said two things: one, \"למה זה שלחתני\" (above 5:22), and the second, \"והצל לא הצלת את עמך\" (ibid. 5:23). And He answered the latter: \"עתה תראה אשר אעשה לפרעה\" (above 6:1), and the former: \"ויאמר אליו אני ד'\" (above 6:2). And the meaning is: through the patriarchs My name was known, which is El Shaddai, and through you My name YHWH, the honored One, is made known in the world, as He said: Therefore say to the children of Israel, I am YHWH. And behold, I have sent you to make this name known."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:47.117483496Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}